   \(f\) is decreasing,

   \[
   f(x)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{x}} \;>\; \frac{1}{\sqrt{k}} = f(k).
   \tag{3.1}
   \]

   (The inequality is strict because the interval contains points
   different from the right‑endpoint \(k\).)

4. **Integrating the pointwise inequality.**  
   Integrating (3.1) over the interval \([k-1,k]\) (which has length
