1. [THEOREM] Numerator-Denominator Relation for Addition of Rational Numbers
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.add_num_den'
Description: For any two rational numbers $q$ and $r$, the numerator of their sum $(q + r).\text{num}$ multiplied by the denominators $q.\text{den}$ and $r.\text{den}$ equals the sum of the cross products $q.\text{num} \cdot r.\text{den} + r.\text{num} \cdot q.\text{den}$ multiplied by the denominator of the sum $(q + r).\text{den}$. In other words:
$$(q + r).\text{num} \cdot q.\text{den} \cdot r.\text{den} = (q.\text{num} \cdot r.\text{den} + r.\text{num} \cdot q.\text{den}) \cdot (q + r).\text{den}.$$
Signature:  (q r : ℚ) : (q + r).num * q.den * r.den = (q.num * r.den + r.num * q.den) * (q + r).den

2. [THEOREM] Numerator of One Equals One
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.num_one
