Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.FundThmCalculus
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt_of_le
Description: Let $a \leq b$ be real numbers, and let $f \colon [a, b] \to E$ be a continuous function on the closed interval $[a, b]$. Suppose that for every $x \in (a, b)$, the function $f$ has a derivative $f'(x)$ at $x$, and that $f'$ is integrable on $[a, b]$. Then:
