Name: derivWithin_mem_iff
Description: For a function $f : \mathbb{K} \to F$, a set $t \subseteq \mathbb{K}$, a point $x \in \mathbb{K}$, and a subset $s \subseteq F$, the derivative of $f$ within $t$ at $x$ belongs to $s$ if and only if either:
1. $f$ is differentiable within $t$ at $x$ and $\text{derivWithin}\, f\, t\, x \in s$, or
2. $f$ is not differentiable within $t$ at $x$ and $0 \in s$.

In mathematical notation:
\[
\text{derivWithin}\, f\, t\, x \in s \leftrightarrow 
\begin{cases}
\text{DifferentiableWithinAt}\, \mathbb{K}\, f\, t\, x \land \text{derivWithin}\, f\, t\, x \in s \\
\lor \\
\neg \text{DifferentiableWithinAt}\, \mathbb{K}\, f\, t\, x \land 0 \in s
\end{cases}
\]
