1. [THEOREM] Square Root of Squared Nonnegative Real Number Equals Original Number
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_mul_self
Description: For any real number $x \geq 0$, the square root of $x^2$ equals $x$, i.e., $\sqrt{x^2} = x$.
Signature:  (h : 0 ≤ x) : √(x * x) = x

2. [THEOREM] Square Root of Squared Real Number Equals Absolute Value: $\sqrt{x^2} = |x|$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_mul_self_eq_abs
Description: For any real number $x$, the square root of $x^2$ equals the absolute value of $x$, i.e., $\sqrt{x^2} = |x|$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) : √(x * x) = |x|

3. [THEOREM] Differentiability of Square Root at Nonzero Points: $\sqrt{x}$ has derivative $\frac{1}{2\sqrt{x}}$ for $x \neq 0$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Sqrt
Name: Real.hasDerivAt_sqrt
Description: For any real number $x \neq 0$, the square root function $\sqrt{\cdot}$ is differentiable at $x$ with derivative $\frac{1}{2\sqrt{x}}$.
Signature:  {x : ℝ} (hx : x ≠ 0) : HasDerivAt (√·) (1 / (2 * √x)) x

4. [THEOREM] Fundamental Theorem of Calculus: $\int_a^b f' = f(b) - f(a)$ for functions differentiable on $\text{uIcc}(a, b)$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.FundThmCalculus
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt
Description: Let $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function such that for every $x$ in the closed interval $\text{uIcc}(a, b)$ (the smallest interval containing $a$ and $b$), $f$ has a derivative $f'(x)$ at $x$, and $f'$ is integrable on $[a, b]$. Then:
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f'(y) \, dy = f(b) - f(a). \]
Signature:  (hderiv : ∀ x ∈ uIcc a b, HasDerivAt f (f' x) x) (hint : IntervalIntegrable f' volume a b) :
  ∫ y in a..b, f' y = f b - f a
