Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegrable_iff_integrableOn_Ioc_of_le
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$, a function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ is interval integrable with respect to measure $\mu$ on $[a, b]$ if and only if $f$ is integrable on the half-open interval $(a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$.
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b ↔ IntegrableOn f (Ioc a b) μ

2. [THEOREM] Square Root Preserves Strict Inequality for Nonnegative Inputs
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_lt_sqrt
Description: For any real numbers $x$ and $y$ with $x \geq 0$, if $x < y$ then $\sqrt{x} < \sqrt{y}$.
Signature:  (hx : 0 ≤ x) (h : x < y) : √x < √y

3. [THEOREM] Positivity of Square Root: $\sqrt{x} > 0 \leftrightarrow x > 0$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_pos
Description: For any real number $x$, the square root of $x$ is positive if and only if $x$ is positive, i.e., $\sqrt{x} > 0 \leftrightarrow x > 0$.
Signature:  : 0 < √x ↔ 0 < x

4. [THEOREM] Integrability condition for $x^{-1}$: $a = b$ or $0 \notin [a, b]$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.NonIntegrable
Name: intervalIntegrable_inv_iff
Description: The function $f(x) = x^{-1}$ is interval integrable on $[a, b]$ with respect to the Lebesgue measure if and only if either $a = b$ or $0$ does not belong to the closed interval $[a, b]$.
Signature:  {a b : ℝ} : IntervalIntegrable (fun x => x⁻¹) volume a b ↔ a = b ∨ (0 : ℝ) ∉ [[a, b]]

5. [THEOREM] Interval Integrability of Constant Functions under Locally Finite Measures
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegrable_const
Description: Let $\mu$ be a locally finite measure on $\mathbb{R}$. For any constant function $f(x) = c$ where $c \in E$, the function $f$ is interval integrable on any interval $[a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$.
Signature:  [IsLocallyFiniteMeasure μ] {c : E} : IntervalIntegrable (fun _ => c) μ a b

6. [THEOREM] Square Root Vanishes if and only if Argument is Nonpositive
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_eq_zero'
Description: For any real number $x$, the square root of $x$ equals zero if and only if $x$ is less than or equal to zero, i.e., $\sqrt{x} = 0 \leftrightarrow x \leq 0$.
Signature:  : √x = 0 ↔ x ≤ 0

7. [THEOREM] Nonzero Square Root if and only if Nonzero Argument for Nonnegative Reals
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_ne_zero
Description: For any nonnegative real number $x \geq 0$, the square root of $x$ is nonzero if and only if $x$ is nonzero, i.e., $\sqrt{x} \neq 0 \leftrightarrow x \neq 0$.
Signature:  (h : 0 ≤ x) : √x ≠ 0 ↔ x ≠ 0
