1. [THEOREM] Numerator of Natural Number Cast to Rationals Equals Original Number
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.num_ofNat
Description: For any natural number $n$, the numerator of the rational number constructed from $n$ (denoted as $\text{ofNat}(n)$) is equal to $n$ itself, i.e., $\text{num}(\text{ofNat}(n)) = n$.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : num ofNat(n) = ofNat(n)

2. [THEOREM] Division Formula for Rational Numbers: $q / r = (n_q d_r)/(d_q n_r)$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.div_def'
Description: For any rational numbers $q$ and $r$, the division $q / r$ is equal to the fraction $(q.\text{num} \cdot r.\text{den}) / (q.\text{den} \cdot r.\text{num})$, where $q.\text{num}$ and $q.\text{den}$ are the numerator and denominator of $q$, and similarly for $r$.
Signature:  (q r : ℚ) : q / r = (q.num * r.den) /. (q.den * r.num)

3. [THEOREM] Numerator Formula for Reduced Rational Number: $\text{num}(n/d) = \frac{\text{sign}(d) \cdot n}{\gcd(n, d)}$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Lemmas
Name: Rat.num_mk
Description: For any integers $n$ and $d$, the numerator of the reduced form of the rational number $n/d$ is equal to $\text{sign}(d) \cdot n$ divided by the greatest common divisor of $n$ and $d$, i.e.,
\[ \text{num}(n/d) = \frac{\text{sign}(d) \cdot n}{\gcd(n, d)}. \]
Signature:  (n d : ℤ) : (n /. d).num = d.sign * n / n.gcd d

4. [THEOREM] Numerator of One Equals One
Module: Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
Name: Rat.num_one
Description: The numerator of the rational number $1$ is equal to $1$, i.e., $\text{num}(1) = 1$.
Signature:  : (1 : ℚ).num = 1
