1. [THEOREM] Sine Periodicity with Natural Multiples of $\pi$: $\sin(x + n\pi) = (-1)^n \sin x$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic
Name: Real.sin_add_nat_mul_pi
Description: For any real number $x$ and natural number $n$, the sine function satisfies $\sin(x + n\pi) = (-1)^n \sin x$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) (n : ℕ) : sin (x + n * π) = (-1) ^ n * sin x

2. [THEOREM] Sine Function Periodicity with Integer Multiples of $\pi$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic
Name: Real.sin_sub_nat_mul_pi
Description: For any real number $x$ and natural number $n$, the sine function satisfies $\sin(x - n\pi) = (-1)^n \sin x$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) (n : ℕ) : sin (x - n * π) = (-1) ^ n * sin x

3. [THEOREM] Cosine-Sine Phase Shift Identity: $\cos(x - \pi/2) = \sin x$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic
Name: Real.cos_sub_pi_div_two
Description: For any real number $x$, the cosine of $x - \pi/2$ equals the sine of $x$, i.e., $\cos(x - \frac{\pi}{2}) = \sin x$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) : cos (x - π / 2) = sin x

4. [THEOREM] Sine Addition Formula for Angles Modulo $2\pi$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Angle
Name: Real.Angle.sin_add
Description: For any two angles $\theta_1$ and $\theta_2$ in $\mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}$, the sine of their sum satisfies the identity:
\[ \sin(\theta_1 + \theta_2) = \sin \theta_1 \cos \theta_2 + \cos \theta_1 \sin \theta_2. \]
Signature:  (θ₁ θ₂ : Real.Angle) : sin (θ₁ + θ₂) = sin θ₁ * cos θ₂ + cos θ₁ * sin θ₂

5. [THEOREM] Cosine-Sine Complementary Angle Identity: $\cos(\pi/2 - x) = \sin x$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic
Name: Real.cos_pi_div_two_sub
Description: For any real number $x$, the cosine of $\frac{\pi}{2} - x$ equals the sine of $x$, i.e., $\cos\left(\frac{\pi}{2} - x\right) = \sin x$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) : cos (π / 2 - x) = sin x

6. [THEOREM] Sine Shift Identity: $\sin(x - \pi/2) = -\cos x$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Basic
Name: Real.sin_sub_pi_div_two
Description: For any real number $x$, the sine function evaluated at $x - \pi/2$ equals the negative cosine of $x$, i.e., $\sin(x - \pi/2) = -\cos x$.
Signature:  (x : ℝ) : sin (x - π / 2) = -cos x
