**Goal.**  
Show that  

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{35}\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{5k\pi}{180}\Bigr)=\tan\!\Bigl(\frac{35\pi}{72}\Bigr).
\]

---

### 1.  Rewrite the angles in radians  

\[
\frac{5k\pi}{180}=k\cdot\frac{\pi}{36}\qquad(k\in\mathbb N).
\]

Hence set  

\[
\theta:=\frac{\pi}{36}\;(=5^\circ),\qquad\text{so that}\qquad 
\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{5k\pi}{180}\Bigr)=\sin(k\theta).
\]

The statement becomes  

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{35}\sin(k\theta)=\tan\!\Bigl(\frac{35\pi}{72}\Bigr).
\tag{1}
\]

---

### 2.  Use the standard finite‑sum formula for sines  

For any real \(\theta\neq 0\) and any integer \(n\ge 1\),

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{n}\sin(k\theta)=
\frac{\sin\!\bigl(\frac{n\theta}{2}\bigr)\,
      \sin\!\bigl(\frac{(n+1)\theta}{2}\bigr)}
     {\sin\!\bigl(\frac{\theta}{2}\bigr)}.
\tag{2}
\]

*Proof of (2).*  
Write the sum as the imaginary part of a geometric series:

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{n}e^{ik\theta}=e^{i\theta}\frac{1-e^{in\theta}}{1-e^{i\theta}}
 =e^{i\frac{(n+1)\theta}{2}}\frac{\sin\!\bigl(\frac{n\theta}{2}\bigr)}
                               {\sin\!\bigl(\frac{\theta}{2}\bigr)} .
\]

Taking imaginary parts and using \(\Im(e^{i\alpha})=\sin\alpha\) yields (2). ∎  

We shall apply (2) with \(n=35\) and \(\theta=\pi/36\).

---

### 3.  Compute the three sine factors appearing in (2)

*First factor*  

\[
\frac{n\theta}{2}= \frac{35}{2}\cdot\frac{\pi}{36}= \frac{35\pi}{72}.
\]

Hence  

\[
\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{n\theta}{2}\Bigr)=\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{35\pi}{72}\Bigr).
\tag{3}
\]

*Second factor*  

\[
\frac{(n+1)\theta}{2}= \frac{36}{2}\cdot\frac{\pi}{36}= \frac{\pi}{2},
\]

so  

\[
\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{(n+1)\theta}{2}\Bigr)=\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{\pi}{2}\Bigr)=1.
\tag{4}
\]

*Denominator*  

\[
\frac{\theta}{2}= \frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{\pi}{36}= \frac{\pi}{72},
\]

hence  

\[
\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{\theta}{2}\Bigr)=\sin\!\Bigl(\frac{\pi}{72}\Bigr).
\tag{5}
\]

---

### 4.  Substitute (3)–(5) into the sum formula (2)

From (2) we obtain

\[
\sum_{k=1}^{35}\sin(k\theta)=
\frac{\sin\!\bigl(\frac{35\pi}{72}\bigr)\cdot 1}
     {\sin\!\bigl(\frac{\pi}{72}\bigr)}
 =\frac{\sin\!\bigl(\frac{35\pi}{72}\bigr)}
