4. [THEOREM] Sine Equality Criterion for Angles Modulo $2\pi$
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Trigonometric.Angle
Name: Real.Angle.sin_eq_iff_coe_eq_or_add_eq_pi
Description: For any real numbers $\theta$ and $\psi$, the sine values $\sin \theta$ and $\sin \psi$ are equal if and only if either:
1. The angles $\theta$ and $\psi$ are equivalent modulo $2\pi$ (i.e., $(\theta : \mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}) = (\psi : \mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z})$), or
2. The sum of the angles $\theta$ and $\psi$ is equivalent to $\pi$ modulo $2\pi$ (i.e., $(\theta : \mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}) + (\psi : \mathbb{R}/2\pi\mathbb{Z}) = \pi$).

Symbolically:
\[ \sin \theta = \sin \psi \iff \theta \equiv \psi \pmod{2\pi} \text{ or } \theta + \psi \equiv \pi \pmod{2\pi}. \]
Signature:  {θ ψ : ℝ} : sin θ = sin ψ ↔ (θ : Angle) = ψ ∨ (θ : Angle) + ψ = π

