1. [THEOREM] Positivity of Square Root: $\sqrt{x} > 0 \leftrightarrow x > 0$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_pos
Description: For any real number $x$, the square root of $x$ is positive if and only if $x$ is positive, i.e., $\sqrt{x} > 0 \leftrightarrow x > 0$.
Signature:  : 0 < √x ↔ 0 < x

2. [THEOREM] Sum of Antitone Function Values at Right Endpoints is Bounded by Integral
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: AntitoneOn.sum_le_integral
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be an antitone (decreasing) function on the interval $[x_0, x_0 + a]$. Then the sum of the values of $f$ at the points $x_0 + (i + 1)$ for $i$ from $0$ to $a-1$ is less than or equal to the integral of $f$ over the interval $[x_0, x_0 + a]$, i.e.,
\[
\sum_{i=0}^{a-1} f(x_0 + i + 1) \leq \int_{x_0}^{x_0 + a} f(x) \, dx.
\]
Signature:  (hf : AntitoneOn f (Icc x₀ (x₀ + a))) : (∑ i ∈ Finset.range a, f (x₀ + (i + 1 : ℕ))) ≤ ∫ x in x₀..x₀ + a, f x

3. [THEOREM] Interval Integral Equals Scaled Integral Over Union Interval: $\int_a^b f = \pm \int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.intervalIntegral_eq_integral_uIoc
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$ and any measurable function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$, the interval integral $\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu$ equals the integral of $f$ over the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, scaled by $1$ if $a \leq b$ and by $-1$ otherwise. That is,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu = \begin{cases}
\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu & \text{if } a \leq b \\
-\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases} \]
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b : ℝ) (μ : Measure ℝ) : ∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ = (if a ≤ b then 1 else -1 : ℝ) • ∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ

4. [THEOREM] Integral of Antitone Function Bounded by Sum Over Integer Points
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: AntitoneOn.integral_le_sum
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be an antitone (decreasing) function on the interval $[x_0, x_0 + a]$. Then the integral of $f$ over $[x_0, x_0 + a]$ is bounded above by the sum of $f$ evaluated at the integer points $x_0, x_0 + 1, \ldots, x_0 + (a - 1)$, i.e.,
\[
\int_{x_0}^{x_0 + a} f(x) \, dx \leq \sum_{i=0}^{a-1} f(x_0 + i).
\]
Signature:  (hf : AntitoneOn f (Icc x₀ (x₀ + a))) : (∫ x in x₀..x₀ + a, f x) ≤ ∑ i ∈ Finset.range a, f (x₀ + i)

5. [THEOREM] Possible Values of Interval Integral: $\int_a^b f \in \{\pm \int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f\}$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_cases
Description: For any measurable function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ and real numbers $a, b$, the interval integral $\int_a^b f(x) \, d\mu$ is either equal to $\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$ or to its negation $-\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$, where $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$ denotes the interval between $a$ and $b$.
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b) : (∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ) ∈ ({∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ, -∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ} : Set E)

6. [THEOREM] Negation of Interval Integral: $\int_a^b -f = -\int_a^b f$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_neg
Description: For any function $f$ defined on the interval $[a,b]$, the integral of $-f$ over $[a,b]$ with respect to measure $\mu$ equals the negation of the integral of $f$ over the same interval, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} -f(x) \, d\mu = -\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  : ∫ x in a..b, -f x ∂μ = -∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ
