1. [THEOREM] Constant Functions are Antitone on Any Subset
Module: Mathlib.Order.Monotone.Basic
Name: antitoneOn_const
Description: For any constant function $f \colon \alpha \to \beta$ between two preorders, where $f(x) = c$ for some fixed $c \in \beta$, and for any subset $s \subseteq \alpha$, the function $f$ is antitone on $s$. That is, for all $a, b \in s$, if $a \leq b$, then $c \leq c$.
Signature:  [Preorder α] [Preorder β] {c : β} {s : Set α} : AntitoneOn (fun _ : α ↦ c) s

2. [THEOREM] Reciprocal Identity for Square Root: $\frac{\sqrt{x}}{x} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_div_self'
Description: For any real number $x$, the quotient of the square root of $x$ divided by $x$ equals the reciprocal of the square root of $x$, i.e., $\frac{\sqrt{x}}{x} = \frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}$.
Signature:  : √x / x = 1 / √x

3. [THEOREM] Closed Interval Subset Criterion: $[a_1, b_1] \subseteq [a_2, b_2] \iff a_2 \leq a_1 \wedge b_1 \leq b_2$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.Basic
Name: Set.Icc_subset_Icc_iff
Description: For elements $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ in a preorder $\alpha$ with $a_1 \leq b_1$, the closed interval $[a_1, b_1]$ is a subset of the closed interval $[a_2, b_2]$ if and only if $a_2 \leq a_1$ and $b_1 \leq b_2$.
Signature:  (h₁ : a₁ ≤ b₁) : Icc a₁ b₁ ⊆ Icc a₂ b₂ ↔ a₂ ≤ a₁ ∧ b₁ ≤ b₂

4. [THEOREM] Quotient Identity: $x / \sqrt{x} = \sqrt{x}$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.div_sqrt
Description: For any real number $x$, the quotient of $x$ divided by its square root equals the square root of $x$, i.e., $x / \sqrt{x} = \sqrt{x}$.
Signature:  : x / √x = √x

5. [THEOREM] Nonzero Interval Integral Implies Interval Integrability
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.intervalIntegrable_of_integral_ne_zero
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$, and any function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, if the interval integral $\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu$ is nonzero, then $f$ is interval integrable with respect to the measure $\mu$ on the interval from $a$ to $b$.
Signature:  {a b : ℝ} {f : ℝ → E} {μ : Measure ℝ} (h : (∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ) ≠ 0) : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b

