1. [THEOREM] Interval integrability criterion for $a \leq b$: $f$ integrable on $[a,b]$ iff integrable on $(a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegrable_iff_integrableOn_Ioc_of_le
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$, a function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ is interval integrable with respect to measure $\mu$ on $[a, b]$ if and only if $f$ is integrable on the half-open interval $(a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$.
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b ↔ IntegrableOn f (Ioc a b) μ

2. [THEOREM] Lebesgue Measure of Interval: $\text{volume}(\text{uIcc}(a, b)) = |b - a|$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic
Name: Real.volume_interval
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$, the Lebesgue measure of the interval $\text{uIcc}(a, b)$ (the closed interval between $a$ and $b$) is equal to the absolute value of their difference, $|b - a|$.
Signature:  {a b : ℝ} : volume (uIcc a b) = ofReal |b - a|

3. [THEOREM] Interval Integral Equals Full Integral When Support is Contained in Interval
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_eq_integral_of_support_subset
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$, if the support of a function $f$ is contained in the half-open interval $(a, b]$, then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ with respect to measure $\mu$ equals the integral of $f$ over the entire space, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu = \int_{\mathbb{R}} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  {a b} (h : support f ⊆ Ioc a b) : ∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ = ∫ x, f x ∂μ

4. [THEOREM] Norm Bound for Interval Integral under Almost Everywhere Constraint: $\|\int_a^b f\| \leq C|b-a|$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const_ae
Description: For any real numbers $a, b$ and any function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, if there exists a constant $C$ such that $\|f(x)\| \leq C$ for almost every $x$ in the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, then the norm of the integral of $f$ over $[a,b]$ satisfies
\[ \left\| \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx \right\| \leq C \cdot |b - a|. \]
Signature:  {a b C : ℝ} {f : ℝ → E} (h : ∀ᵐ x, x ∈ Ι a b → ‖f x‖ ≤ C) : ‖∫ x in a..b, f x‖ ≤ C * |b - a|

5. [THEOREM] Norm Bound for Interval Integral: $\|\int_a^b f\| \leq C|b-a|$ under Uniform Constraint
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.norm_integral_le_of_norm_le_const
Description: For any real numbers $a, b$, any function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, and any constant $C \in \mathbb{R}$, if $\|f(x)\| \leq C$ for all $x$ in the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b))$, then the norm of the integral of $f$ over $[a,b]$ satisfies
\[ \left\| \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx \right\| \leq C \cdot |b - a|. \]
Signature:  {a b C : ℝ} {f : ℝ → E} (h : ∀ x ∈ Ι a b, ‖f x‖ ≤ C) : ‖∫ x in a..b, f x‖ ≤ C * |b - a|

6. [THEOREM] Lebesgue measure of closed interval: $\text{volume}([a, b]) = b - a$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Lebesgue.Basic
Name: Real.volume_Icc
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$, the Lebesgue measure of the closed interval $[a, b]$ is equal to $b - a$.
Signature:  {a b : ℝ} : volume (Icc a b) = ofReal (b - a)
