5. [THEOREM] Zero Restriction Characterization: $\mu|_A = 0 \leftrightarrow \mu(A) = 0$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.FiniteMeasure
Name: MeasureTheory.FiniteMeasure.restrict_eq_zero_iff
Description: For any finite measure $\mu$ on a measurable space $\Omega$ and any measurable set $A \subseteq \Omega$, the restriction of $\mu$ to $A$ is the zero measure if and only if $\mu(A) = 0$. In other words, $\mu|_A = 0 \leftrightarrow \mu(A) = 0$.
