1. [THEOREM] Sum of Antitone Function at Right Endpoints is Bounded by Integral over Interval
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.SumIntegralComparisons
Name: AntitoneOn.sum_le_integral_Ico
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{R}$ be an antitone (decreasing) function on the closed interval $[a, b]$, where $a \leq b$. Then the sum of the values of $f$ at the right endpoints of the integer subintervals in $[a, b)$, i.e., $f(i+1)$ for each integer $i$ in the half-open interval $[a, b)$, is less than or equal to the integral of $f$ over $[a, b]$. Mathematically, this is expressed as:
\[
\sum_{i \in [a, b) \cap \mathbb{Z}} f(i+1) \leq \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, dx.
\]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hf : AntitoneOn f (Set.Icc a b)) : (∑ i ∈ Finset.Ico a b, f (i + 1 : ℕ)) ≤ ∫ x in a..b, f x

2. [THEOREM] Inclusion Condition for Closed Finset Interval in Closed-Open Finset Interval: $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁) \subseteq \text{Ico}(a₂, b₂) \leftrightarrow a₂ \leq a₁ \land b₁ < b₂$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_subset_Ico_iff
Description: For any elements $a₁, b₁, a₂, b₂$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a₁ \leq b₁$, the finset $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁)$ is a subset of the finset $\text{Ico}(a₂, b₂)$ if and only if $a₂ \leq a₁$ and $b₁ < b₂$.
Signature:  (h₁ : a₁ ≤ b₁) : Icc a₁ b₁ ⊆ Ico a₂ b₂ ↔ a₂ ≤ a₁ ∧ b₁ < b₂

3. [THEOREM] Difference of Closed and Closed-Open Interval Finsets: $\text{Icc}(a,b) \setminus \text{Ico}(a,b) = \{b\}$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_diff_Ico_self
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a \leq b$, the set difference between the finsets $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ and $\text{Ico}(a, b)$ is the singleton finset $\{b\}$. In other words, $\text{Icc}(a, b) \setminus \text{Ico}(a, b) = \{b\}$.
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) : Icc a b \ Ico a b = { b }
