1. [THEOREM] Evaluation of Finite Sum of Dependently-Typed Functions is Pointwise Sum of Evaluations
Module: Mathlib.Data.DFinsupp.BigOperators
Name: DFinsupp.finset_sum_apply
Description: For any family of additive commutative monoids $(\beta_i)_{i \in \iota}$, any finite set $s$ of elements of type $\alpha$, and any function $g \colon \alpha \to \Pi_{i \in \iota} \beta_i$ mapping each element of $\alpha$ to a dependently-typed function with finite support, the evaluation at index $i$ of the sum $\sum_{a \in s} g(a)$ equals the sum $\sum_{a \in s} g(a)(i)$ for each $i \in \iota$.
Signature:  {α} [∀ i, AddCommMonoid (β i)] (s : Finset α) (g : α → Π₀ i, β i) (i : ι) : (∑ a ∈ s, g a) i = ∑ a ∈ s, g a i

2. [THEOREM] Sum of Indicator-Weighted Terms in a Finite Set: $\sum_{j \in s} \mathbb{1}_{\{i = j\}} f(j) = f(i) \mathbb{1}_{\{i \in s\}}$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring
Name: Finset.sum_boole_mul
Description: For any finite set $s$ of indices, any function $f : \iota \to \alpha$ (where $\alpha$ is a non-associative semiring), and any index $i \in \iota$, the sum $\sum_{j \in s} \mathbb{1}_{\{i = j\}} \cdot f(j)$ equals $f(i)$ if $i \in s$ and $0$ otherwise. Here $\mathbb{1}_{\{i = j\}}$ is the indicator function that equals $1$ when $i = j$ and $0$ otherwise.
Signature:  (s : Finset ι) (f : ι → α) (i : ι) : ∑ j ∈ s, ite (i = j) 1 0 * f j = ite (i ∈ s) (f i) 0

3. [THEOREM] Finset Coefficients of Closed Interval Equal Set Interval
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Defs
Name: Finset.coe_Icc
Description: For any elements $a, b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the underlying set of the finset $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ is equal to the closed interval $\{x \in \alpha \mid a \leq x \leq b\}$.
Signature:  (a b : α) : (Icc a b : Set α) = Set.Icc a b

4. [THEOREM] Sum of Indicator Single Functions Equals Single Function
Module: Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.VectorSpace
Name: Finset.sum_single_ite
Description: Let $n$ be a finite type, $R$ a ring, and $a \in R$. For any $i \in n$, the sum over $x \in n$ of the function sending $x$ to the finite support function $\text{single}_x(a)$ if $x = i$ and to the zero function otherwise, equals the finite support function $\text{single}_i(a)$. In mathematical notation:
\[ \sum_{x \in n} \text{single}_x \Big( \begin{cases} 
a & \text{if } x = i \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases} \Big) = \text{single}_i(a) \]
Signature:  [Fintype n] (a : R) (i : n) : (∑ x : n, Finsupp.single x (if i = x then a else 0)) = Finsupp.single i a

5. [THEOREM] Evaluation Commutes with Finite Summation of Functions
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Finsupp
Name: Finset.sum_apply'
Description: For any finite set $s$ and a family of functions $f_k \colon \alpha \to M$ indexed by $k \in s$, the evaluation of the sum of these functions at any point $i \in \alpha$ equals the sum of the evaluations of each function at $i$. That is:
$$ \left(\sum_{k \in s} f_k\right)(i) = \sum_{k \in s} f_k(i) $$
Signature:  : (∑ k ∈ s, f k) i = ∑ k ∈ s, f k i
