1. [THEOREM] Summation Recursion over Antidiagonal: $\sum_{i+j=n+1} f(i,j) = f(n+1,0) + \sum_{i+j=n} f(i,j+1)$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.NatAntidiagonal
Name: Finset.Nat.sum_antidiagonal_succ'
Description: For any natural number $n$ and any function $f \colon \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{N} \to N$ where $N$ is an additive commutative monoid, the sum of $f$ over the antidiagonal set $\{(i,j) \mid i + j = n+1\}$ satisfies:
\[
\sum_{(i,j) \in \text{antidiagonal}(n+1)} f(i,j) = f(n+1, 0) + \sum_{(i,j) \in \text{antidiagonal}(n)} f(i, j+1).
\]
Signature:  {n : ℕ} {f : ℕ × ℕ → N} : (∑ p ∈ antidiagonal (n + 1), f p) = f (n + 1, 0) + ∑ p ∈ antidiagonal n, f (p.1, p.2 + 1)

2. [THEOREM] Sum over Antidiagonal Recursion: $\sum_{i+j=n+1} f(i,j) = f(0,n+1) + \sum_{i+j=n} f(i+1,j)$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.NatAntidiagonal
Name: Finset.Nat.sum_antidiagonal_succ
Description: For any natural number $n$ and any function $f \colon \mathbb{N} \times \mathbb{N} \to N$ where $N$ is an additive commutative monoid, the sum of $f$ over the antidiagonal set $\{(i,j) \mid i + j = n+1\}$ satisfies:
\[
\sum_{(i,j) \in \text{antidiagonal}(n+1)} f(i,j) = f(0, n+1) + \sum_{(i,j) \in \text{antidiagonal}(n)} f(i+1, j).
\]
Signature:  {n : ℕ} {f : ℕ × ℕ → N} : (∑ p ∈ antidiagonal (n + 1), f p) = f (0, n + 1) + ∑ p ∈ antidiagonal n, f (p.1 + 1, p.2)

3. [THEOREM] Summation by Parts Formula for Finite Intervals: $\sum_{i=m}^{n-1} f(i)g(i) = f(n-1)G(n) - f(m)G(m) - \sum_{i=m}^{n-2} (f(i+1)-f(i))G(i+1)$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Module
Name: Finset.sum_Ico_by_parts
Description: Let $m$ and $n$ be natural numbers with $m < n$, and let $f : \mathbb{N} → R$ and $g : \mathbb{N} → R$ be sequences in a ring $R$. Define $G(k) = \sum_{i=m}^{k-1} g(i)$ for $k > m$ and $G(m) = 0$. Then the following summation by parts formula holds:

$$
\sum_{i=m}^{n-1} f(i) g(i) = f(n-1) G(n) - f(m) G(m) - \sum_{i=m}^{n-2} (f(i+1) - f(i)) G(i+1)
$$
Signature:  (hmn : m < n) :
  ∑ i ∈ Ico m n, f i • g i = f (n - 1) • G n - f m • G m - ∑ i ∈ Ico m (n - 1), (f (i + 1) - f i) • G (i + 1)

4. [THEOREM] Summation by Parts Formula for Open-Closed Intervals: $\sum_{i=m+1}^n f(i)g(i) = f(n)G(n+1) - f(m+1)G(m+1) - \sum_{i=m+1}^{n-1} (f(i+1)-f(i))G(i+1)$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Module
Name: Finset.sum_Ioc_by_parts
Description: Let $m$ and $n$ be natural numbers with $m < n$, and let $f : \mathbb{N} \to R$ and $g : \mathbb{N} \to R$ be sequences in a ring $R$. Define $G(k) = \sum_{i=m}^{k-1} g(i)$ for $k > m$ and $G(m) = 0$. Then the following summation by parts formula holds for the open-closed interval $(m, n]$:

$$
\sum_{i=m+1}^n f(i) g(i) = f(n) G(n+1) - f(m+1) G(m+1) - \sum_{i=m+1}^{n-1} (f(i+1) - f(i)) G(i+1)
$$
Signature:  (hmn : m < n) :
  ∑ i ∈ Ioc m n, f i • g i =
    f n • G (n + 1) - f (m + 1) • G (m + 1) - ∑ i ∈ Ioc m (n - 1), (f (i + 1) - f i) • G (i + 1)
