Description: For any finite set $s$ of indices, any function $f : \iota \to \alpha$ (where $\alpha$ is a non-associative semiring), and any index $i \in \iota$, the sum $\sum_{j \in s} \mathbb{1}_{\{i = j\}} \cdot f(j)$ equals $f(i)$ if $i \in s$ and $0$ otherwise. Here $\mathbb{1}_{\{i = j\}}$ is the indicator function that equals $1$ when $i = j$ and $0$ otherwise.
Signature:  (s : Finset ι) (f : ι → α) (i : ι) : ∑ j ∈ s, ite (i = j) 1 0 * f j = ite (i ∈ s) (f i) 0

2. [THEOREM] Additivity of Integral Sums: \(\text{integralSum}(f + g) = \text{integralSum}(f) + \text{integralSum}(g)\)
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Basic
Name: BoxIntegral.integralSum_add
Description: For any two functions \( f, g : \mathbb{R}^n \to E \), a box-additive volume function \(\text{vol}\) mapping boxes in \(\mathbb{R}^n\) to continuous linear maps from \(E\) to \(F\), and a tagged prepartition \(\pi\) of a box \(I\), the integral sum of the sum \(f + g\) over \(\pi\) with respect to \(\text{vol}\) is equal to the sum of the integral sums of \(f\) and \(g\) over \(\pi\) with respect to \(\text{vol}\). That is,
\[
\text{integralSum}(f + g, \text{vol}, \pi) = \text{integralSum}(f, \text{vol}, \pi) + \text{integralSum}(g, \text{vol}, \pi).
\]
Signature:  (f g : ℝⁿ → E) (vol : ι →ᵇᵃ E →L[ℝ] F) (π : TaggedPrepartition I) :
  integralSum (f + g) vol π = integralSum f vol π + integralSum g vol π

3. [THEOREM] Inclusion Condition for Closed Finset Interval in Closed-Open Finset Interval: $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁) \subseteq \text{Ico}(a₂, b₂) \leftrightarrow a₂ \leq a₁ \land b₁ < b₂$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_subset_Ico_iff
Description: For any elements $a₁, b₁, a₂, b₂$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a₁ \leq b₁$, the finset $\text{Icc}(a₁, b₁)$ is a subset of the finset $\text{Ico}(a₂, b₂)$ if and only if $a₂ \leq a₁$ and $b₁ < b₂$.
Signature:  (h₁ : a₁ ≤ b₁) : Icc a₁ b₁ ⊆ Ico a₂ b₂ ↔ a₂ ≤ a₁ ∧ b₁ < b₂

4. [THEOREM] Equality of Lower-Closed Interval and Closed Interval from Bottom Element
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Defs
Name: Finset.Iic_eq_Icc
Description: In a locally finite order $\alpha$ with a bottom element $\bot$, the finset of elements less than or equal to $b$ is equal to the closed interval from $\bot$ to $b$, i.e., $\text{Iic}(b) = \text{Icc}(\bot, b)$ for any $b \in \alpha$.
Signature:  : Iic = Icc (⊥ : α)

5. [THEOREM] Sum of Cons Function Equals Element Plus Sum of Tail
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Finsupp
Name: Finsupp.sum_cons
Description: Let $M$ be an additively commutative monoid. For any natural number $n$, finitely supported function $\sigma \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,n \to_0 M$, and element $i \in M$, the sum of the elements of the finitely supported function $\mathrm{cons}\,i\,\sigma \colon \mathrm{Fin}\,(n+1) \to_0 M$ is equal to $i$ plus the sum of the elements of $\sigma$. 

In mathematical notation:
$$\sum_{x \in \mathrm{Fin}\,(n+1)} (\mathrm{cons}\,i\,\sigma)(x) = i + \sum_{x \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n} \sigma(x)$$
Signature:  [AddCommMonoid M] (n : ℕ) (σ : Fin n →₀ M) (i : M) : (sum (cons i σ) fun _ e ↦ e) = i + sum σ (fun _ e ↦ e)

