1. [THEOREM] Sum of Integrals over Adjacent Subintervals Equals Integral over Entire Interval: $\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \int_{a_k}^{a_{k+1}} f = \int_{a_0}^{a_n} f$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.sum_integral_adjacent_intervals
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function, $\mu$ a measure on $\mathbb{R}$, and $(a_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}}$ a sequence of real numbers. For any natural number $n$, if $f$ is interval integrable on each subinterval $[a_k, a_{k+1}]$ for all $k < n$, then the sum of the integrals over these subintervals equals the integral over the entire interval $[a_0, a_n]$, i.e.,
\[
\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \int_{a_k}^{a_{k+1}} f(x) \, d\mu = \int_{a_0}^{a_n} f(x) \, d\mu.
\]
Signature:  {a : ℕ → ℝ} {n : ℕ} (hint : ∀ k < n, IntervalIntegrable f μ (a k) (a <| k + 1)) :
  ∑ k ∈ Finset.range n, ∫ x in a k..a <| k + 1, f x ∂μ = ∫ x in (a 0)..(a n), f x ∂μ

2. [THEOREM] Interval integral over ordered endpoints equals integral over half-open interval
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_of_le
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$ with $a \leq b$, the interval integral $\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu$ is equal to the integral of $f$ over the half-open interval $(a, b]$, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu = \int_{(a,b]} f(x) \, d\mu. \]
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) : ∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ = ∫ x in Ioc a b, f x ∂μ
