3. [THEOREM] Scaling Property of Interval Integral: $\int_{a}^{b} f(cx) \, dx = c^{-1} \int_{ca}^{cb} f(x) \, dx$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_comp_mul_left
Description: For any nonzero real number $c \neq 0$ and any integrable function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$, the integral of $f(c \cdot x)$ over the interval $[a, b]$ is equal to $c^{-1}$ times the integral of $f(x)$ over the scaled interval $[c \cdot a, c \cdot b]$. That is,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(c \cdot x) \, dx = c^{-1} \cdot \int_{c \cdot a}^{c \cdot b} f(x) \, dx. \]
Signature:  (hc : c ≠ 0) : (∫ x in a..b, f (c * x)) = c⁻¹ • ∫ x in c * a..c * b, f x

4. [THEOREM] Interval Integral Equals Scaled Integral Over Union Interval: $\int_a^b f = \pm \int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.intervalIntegral_eq_integral_uIoc
Description: For any real numbers $a$ and $b$ and any measurable function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$, the interval integral $\int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu$ equals the integral of $f$ over the interval $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$, scaled by $1$ if $a \leq b$ and by $-1$ otherwise. That is,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(x) \, d\mu = \begin{cases}
\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu & \text{if } a \leq b \\
-\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu & \text{otherwise.}
\end{cases} \]
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b : ℝ) (μ : Measure ℝ) : ∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ = (if a ≤ b then 1 else -1 : ℝ) • ∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ

5. [THEOREM] Reflection Property of Interval Integral: $\int_{a}^{b} f(d - x) \, dx = \int_{d - b}^{d - a} f(x) \, dx$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_comp_sub_left
Description: For any real number $d$, the integral of the function $f(d - x)$ over the interval $[a, b]$ equals the integral of $f(x)$ over the interval $[d - b, d - a]$. That is,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(d - x) \, dx = \int_{d - b}^{d - a} f(x) \, dx. \]
Signature:  (d) : (∫ x in a..b, f (d - x)) = ∫ x in d - b..d - a, f x

6. [THEOREM] Possible Values of Interval Integral: $\int_a^b f \in \{\pm \int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f\}$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_cases
Description: For any measurable function $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ and real numbers $a, b$, the interval integral $\int_a^b f(x) \, d\mu$ is either equal to $\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$ or to its negation $-\int_{\text{Ι}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$, where $\text{Ι}(a,b) = (\min(a,b), \max(a,b)]$ denotes the interval between $a$ and $b$.
Signature:  (f : ℝ → E) (a b) : (∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ) ∈ ({∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ, -∫ x in Ι a b, f x ∂μ} : Set E)

7. [THEOREM] Negation of Interval Integral: $\int_a^b -f = -\int_a^b f$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_neg
Description: For any function $f$ defined on the interval $[a,b]$, the integral of $-f$ over $[a,b]$ with respect to measure $\mu$ equals the negation of the integral of $f$ over the same interval, i.e.,
