Description: Let $f$ be a function, $\mu$ be a measure on $\mathbb{R}$, and $l$ be a filter. Given:
1. Families of real numbers $\{a_i\}_{i \in \iota}$ and $\{b_i\}_{i \in \iota}$ such that $a_i \to a_0$ and $b_i \to b_0$ as $i$ tends to $l$
2. For each $i$, $f$ is integrable on the half-open interval $(a_i, b_i]$
3. There exists a real number $I$ such that for $i$ sufficiently close to $l$, the integral $\int_{x \in (a_i, b_i]} \|f(x)\| d\mu \leq I$

Then $f$ is integrable on the interval $(a_0, b_0]$.
