Description: For any real numbers $x$ and $y$ with $x \geq 0$, the inequality $\sqrt{x} < \sqrt{y}$ holds if and only if $x < y$.
Signature:  (hx : 0 ≤ x) : √x < √y ↔ x < y

4. [THEOREM] Square Root Order Preservation: $\sqrt{x} \leq \sqrt{y} \leftrightarrow x \leq y$ for $y \geq 0$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
