1. [THEOREM] Square Root Preserves Strict Inequality for Nonnegative Inputs
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_lt_sqrt
Description: For any real numbers $x$ and $y$ with $x \geq 0$, if $x < y$ then $\sqrt{x} < \sqrt{y}$.
Signature:  (hx : 0 ≤ x) (h : x < y) : √x < √y

2. [THEOREM] Square Root Inequality: $\sqrt{x} \leq y \leftrightarrow y \geq 0 \land x \leq y^2$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_le_iff
Description: For any real numbers $x$ and $y$, the inequality $\sqrt{x} \leq y$ holds if and only if $y$ is nonnegative and $x \leq y^2$.
Signature:  : √x ≤ y ↔ 0 ≤ y ∧ x ≤ y ^ 2

3. [THEOREM] Square Root Preserves Strict Inequality for Nonnegative Real Numbers
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_lt_sqrt_iff
Description: For any real numbers $x$ and $y$ with $x \geq 0$, the inequality $\sqrt{x} < \sqrt{y}$ holds if and only if $x < y$.
Signature:  (hx : 0 ≤ x) : √x < √y ↔ x < y

4. [THEOREM] Square Root Order Preservation: $\sqrt{x} \leq \sqrt{y} \leftrightarrow x \leq y$ for $y \geq 0$
Module: Mathlib.Data.Real.Sqrt
Name: Real.sqrt_le_sqrt_iff
Description: For any real numbers $x$ and $y$ with $y \geq 0$, the inequality $\sqrt{x} \leq \sqrt{y}$ holds if and only if $x \leq y$.
Signature:  (hy : 0 ≤ y) : √x ≤ √y ↔ x ≤ y

