1. [THEOREM] Closed Interval as Insertion of Right Endpoint into Closed-Open Interval: $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \text{Ico}(a, b) \cup \{b\}$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_eq_cons_Ico
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a \leq b$, the closed interval $[a, b]$ can be constructed by inserting the right endpoint $b$ into the closed-open interval $[a, b)$. Formally, $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \text{Ico}(a, b).\text{cons}(b, \text{right\_not\_mem\_Ico})$, where $\text{right\_not\_mem\_Ico}$ is the proof that $b \notin \text{Ico}(a, b)$.
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) : Icc a b = (Ico a b).cons b right_not_mem_Ico

2. [THEOREM] Closed Interval Subset Criterion: $[a_1, b_1] \subseteq [a_2, b_2] \iff a_2 \leq a_1 \wedge b_1 \leq b_2$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.Basic
Name: Set.Icc_subset_Icc_iff
Description: For elements $a_1, b_1, a_2, b_2$ in a preorder $\alpha$ with $a_1 \leq b_1$, the closed interval $[a_1, b_1]$ is a subset of the closed interval $[a_2, b_2]$ if and only if $a_2 \leq a_1$ and $b_1 \leq b_2$.
Signature:  (h₁ : a₁ ≤ b₁) : Icc a₁ b₁ ⊆ Icc a₂ b₂ ↔ a₂ ≤ a₁ ∧ b₁ ≤ b₂

3. [THEOREM] Inclusion of Ordered Interval in Unordered Interval: $[a, b] \subseteq [[a, b]]$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.UnorderedInterval
Name: Set.Icc_subset_uIcc
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a lattice $\alpha$, the closed interval $[a, b]$ is a subset of the unordered closed interval $[[a, b]] := [a \sqcap b, a \sqcup b]$.
Signature:  : Icc a b ⊆ [[a, b]]

4. [THEOREM] Right Endpoint Membership in Closed Interval: $b \in [a, b] \leftrightarrow a \leq b$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.right_mem_Icc
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the element $b$ belongs to the closed interval $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ if and only if $a \leq b$.
Signature:  : b ∈ Icc a b ↔ a ≤ b

5. [THEOREM] Empty Closed Interval Finset When Reversed Order: $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \emptyset$ when $b < a$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_eq_empty_of_lt
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, if $b < a$, then the closed interval finset $\text{Icc}(a, b)$ is empty.
Signature:  (h : b < a) : Icc a b = ∅

6. [THEOREM] Singleton Closed Interval: $\text{Icc}(a, a) = \{a\}$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Multiset
Name: Multiset.Icc_self
Description: For any element $a$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$, the closed interval $\text{Icc}(a, a)$ is equal to the multiset $\{a\}$ containing only $a$ itself.
Signature:  (a : α) : Icc a a = { a }
