1. [THEOREM] Evaluation Formula for Interval Extension: $\mathrm{IccExtend}(h, f)(x) = f(\max(a, \min(b, x)))$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Set.ProjIcc
Name: Set.IccExtend_apply
Description: For any linearly ordered type $\alpha$ and elements $a, b \in \alpha$ with $a \leq b$, the extension $\mathrm{IccExtend}(h, f)$ of a function $f \colon [a, b] \to \beta$ satisfies
\[
\mathrm{IccExtend}(h, f)(x) = f\left(\max(a, \min(b, x))\right)
\]
for all $x \in \alpha$, where $\max(a, \min(b, x))$ is guaranteed to lie in $[a, b]$.
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) (f : Icc a b → β) (x : α) :
  IccExtend h f x = f ⟨max a (min b x), le_max_left _ _, max_le h (min_le_left _ _)⟩

