3. [DEFINITION] Integral over an interval
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: term∫_In_.._,_∂_.delab_app.intervalIntegral
Description: The notation $\int_{x \in a..b} f(x) \, d\mu$ represents the integral of function $f$ over the interval from $a$ to $b$ with respect to measure $\mu$, defined as:
- $\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$ when $a \leq b$
- $-\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(b,a)} f(x) \, d\mu$ when $b \leq a$

where $\text{Ioc}(a,b)$ denotes the half-open interval $(a,b]$.
Signature:  : Delab✝

