Module: Mathlib.Topology.UnitInterval
Name: unitInterval.mem_iff_one_sub_mem
Description: For any real number $t$, $t$ belongs to the unit interval $I = [0,1]$ if and only if $1 - t$ also belongs to $I$.
Signature:  {t : ℝ} : t ∈ I ↔ 1 - t ∈ I

5. [DEFINITION] Interval integral of a function between two points
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: term∫_In_.._,_.delab_app.intervalIntegral
Description: The interval integral $\int_{x \in a..b} f(x) \, d\mu$ is defined as the difference $\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu - \int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(b,a)} f(x) \, d\mu$, where $\text{Ioc}(a,b)$ denotes the half-open interval $(a,b]$. When $a \leq b$, this equals $\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(a,b)} f(x) \, d\mu$, and when $b \leq a$, it equals $-\int_{x \in \text{Ioc}(b,a)} f(x) \, d\mu$.
Signature:  : Delab✝
