Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Measure.Haar.OfBasis
Name: instIsAddHaarMeasureVolume
Description: For any finite-dimensional real inner product space $E$ with a Borel measurable space structure, the canonical Lebesgue measure (denoted by `volume`) is an additive Haar measure. This means it is translation-invariant, finite on compact sets, and positive on open sets, with the normalization that the measure of the parallelepiped spanned by any orthonormal basis is 1.
