5. [DEFINITION] Weighted Lebesgue measure on $(0, \infty)$ with density $r^n$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Constructions.HaarToSphere
Name: MeasureTheory.Measure.volumeIoiPow
Description: For a natural number $n$, the measure `volumeIoiPow n` is defined on the open interval $(0, \infty)$ with density function $r \mapsto r^n$ with respect to the Lebesgue measure. 

More precisely, for any measurable set $A \subseteq (0, \infty)$, the measure is given by:
$$\text{volumeIoiPow}\,n\,A = \int_A r^n \,d\lambda(r)$$
where $\lambda$ is the Lebesgue measure on $\mathbb{R}$.
Signature:  (n : ℕ) : Measure (Ioi (0 : ℝ))

