7. [THEOREM] Interval integrability is preserved under division by a scalar
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: IntervalIntegrable.div_const
Description: Let $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to \mathbb{K}$ be a function that is interval integrable with respect to a measure $\mu$ on $[a, b]$, where $\mathbb{K}$ is a normed field. Then for any nonzero $c \in \mathbb{K}$, the function $x \mapsto f(x) / c$ is interval integrable on $[a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$.
Signature:  {𝕜 : Type*} {f : ℝ → 𝕜} [NormedField 𝕜] (h : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b) (c : 𝕜) :
