1. [THEOREM] Additivity of Interval Integrals: $\int_a^b f + \int_b^c f = \int_a^c f$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_add_adjacent_intervals
Description: Let $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function and $\mu$ a measure on $\mathbb{R}$. If $f$ is interval integrable on $[a,b]$ and $[b,c]$, then the sum of the integrals over $[a,b]$ and $[b,c]$ equals the integral over $[a,c]$, i.e.,
\[
\int_a^b f(x) \, d\mu + \int_b^c f(x) \, d\mu = \int_a^c f(x) \, d\mu.
\]
Signature:  (hab : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b) (hbc : IntervalIntegrable f μ b c) :
  ((∫ x in a..b, f x ∂μ) + ∫ x in b..c, f x ∂μ) = ∫ x in a..c, f x ∂μ

1. [THEOREM] Interval integrability criterion for $a \leq b$: $f$ integrable on $[a,b]$ iff integrable on $(a,b]$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegrable_iff_integrableOn_Ioc_of_le
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$, a function $f : \mathbb{R} \to E$ is interval integrable with respect to measure $\mu$ on $[a, b]$ if and only if $f$ is integrable on the half-open interval $(a, b]$ with respect to $\mu$.
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) : IntervalIntegrable f μ a b ↔ IntegrableOn f (Ioc a b) μ

2. [THEOREM] Characterization of Strict Upper Bound in Unit Interval: $x < 1$ in $I$ iff $x < 1$ in $\mathbb{R}$
Module: Mathlib.Topology.UnitInterval
Name: unitInterval.coe_lt_one
Description: For any element $x$ in the unit interval $I = [0,1]$, the real number corresponding to $x$ is less than $1$ if and only if $x$ is not equal to $1$ (i.e., $x$ is strictly less than $1$ in the subtype order).
Signature:  {x : I} : (x : ℝ) < 1 ↔ x < 1

3. [THEOREM] Characterization of Unit Interval Membership via Complement: $t \in [0,1] \leftrightarrow 1-t \in [0,1]$
Module: Mathlib.Topology.UnitInterval
Name: unitInterval.mem_iff_one_sub_mem
Description: For any real number $t$, $t$ belongs to the unit interval $I = [0,1]$ if and only if $1 - t$ also belongs to $I$.
Signature:  {t : ℝ} : t ∈ I ↔ 1 - t ∈ I

