Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.DominatedConvergence
Name: intervalIntegral.tsum_intervalIntegral_eq_of_summable_norm
Description: Let $\iota$ be a countable index set and $\{f_i\}_{i \in \iota}$ be a family of continuous functions from $\mathbb{R}$ to a Banach space $E$. If the series $\sum_{i \in \iota} \|f_i\|_{[a,b]}$ is summable, where $\|f_i\|_{[a,b]}$ denotes the supremum norm of $f_i$ restricted to the interval $[a,b]$, then the sum of integrals equals the integral of the sum:
\[
\sum_{i \in \iota} \int_a^b f_i(x) \, dx = \int_a^b \left( \sum_{i \in \iota} f_i(x) \right) dx.
\]
