\[
\int_{1}^{2} \frac{dx}{\sqrt{x}} \;>\; (2-1)\cdot\frac1{\sqrt2}= \frac1{\sqrt2}.
\]

Thus the conclusion \(\displaystyle\int_{1}^{2} \frac{dx}{\sqrt{x}} > \frac1{\sqrt2}\) follows from the given hypotheses. The theorem statement is therefore mathematically correct.
