1. [THEOREM] Union of Restricted Prepartition Equals Intersection with Original Union
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Partition.Basic
Name: BoxIntegral.Prepartition.iUnion_restrict
Description: For a prepartition $\pi$ of a rectangular box $I$ in $\mathbb{R}^n$ and another rectangular box $J \subseteq I$, the union of all subboxes in the restriction $\pi.\text{restrict}(J)$ equals the intersection of $J$ with the union of all subboxes in $\pi$, i.e.,
\[
\bigcup_{K \in \pi.\text{restrict}(J)} K = J \cap \left(\bigcup_{K' \in \pi} K'\right).
\]
Signature:  : (π.restrict J).iUnion = (J : Set (ι → ℝ)) ∩ (π.iUnion)

2. [THEOREM] Membership in Restricted Prepartition via Intersection
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Partition.Basic
Name: BoxIntegral.Prepartition.mem_restrict
Description: For any box $J_1$ in the restriction of a prepartition $\pi$ to a box $J$, there exists a box $J'$ in $\pi$ such that $J_1$ is equal to the infimum (intersection) of $J$ and $J'$ when considered as elements of `WithBot (Box ι)`. Conversely, if such a box $J'$ exists, then $J_1$ belongs to the restriction $\pi.restrict J$.
Signature:  : J₁ ∈ π.restrict J ↔ ∃ J' ∈ π, (J₁ : WithBot (Box ι)) = ↑J ⊓ ↑J'

3. [THEOREM] Restriction to Larger Box Preserves Box Set
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Partition.Basic
Name: BoxIntegral.Prepartition.restrict_boxes_of_le
Description: Let $I$ and $J$ be rectangular boxes in $\mathbb{R}^n$ with $I \subseteq J$, and let $\pi$ be a prepartition of $I$. Then the set of boxes in the restriction $\pi.\text{restrict}(J)$ is equal to the set of boxes in $\pi$, i.e., $\pi.\text{restrict}(J).\text{boxes} = \pi.\text{boxes}$.
Signature:  (π : Prepartition I) (h : I ≤ J) : (π.restrict J).boxes = π.boxes

4. [THEOREM] Restriction of Union Prepartition Equals Indexed Prepartition
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Partition.Basic
Name: BoxIntegral.Prepartition.restrict_biUnion
Description: For a prepartition $\pi$ of a rectangular box $I$ in $\mathbb{R}^n$, a collection of prepartitions $\pi_i$ indexed by subboxes of $I$, and a subbox $J \in \pi$, the restriction of the union prepartition $\pi.\text{biUnion} \pi_i$ to $J$ equals the prepartition $\pi_i(J)$. That is,
\[
(\pi.\text{biUnion} \pi_i).\text{restrict}(J) = \pi_i(J).
\]
Signature:  (πi : ∀ J, Prepartition J) (hJ : J ∈ π) : (π.biUnion πi).restrict J = πi J

5. [THEOREM] Box Ordering via Set Inclusion
Module: Mathlib.Analysis.BoxIntegral.Box.Basic
Name: BoxIntegral.Box.le_def
Description: For two rectangular boxes $I$ and $J$ in $\mathbb{R}^\iota$, the inequality $I \leq J$ holds if and only if every point $x$ that belongs to $I$ also belongs to $J$. In other words, $I \leq J$ is equivalent to the set inclusion $I \subseteq J$ where both boxes are interpreted as subsets of $\mathbb{R}^\iota$.
Signature:  : I ≤ J ↔ ∀ x ∈ I, x ∈ J
