The right‑hand side of the desired inequality is \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\approx 0.707\). Since
\[
2(\sqrt{2}-1) \neq \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}},
\]
the conclusion
\[
\int_{1}^{2} \frac{1}{\sqrt{x}}\,dx \neq \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}
\]
holds. The premise is not needed for the conclusion, but it does not contradict it. Therefore the theorem statement is mathematically correct.
</justification>
