1. [THEOREM] Reflection Property of Interval Integral: $\int_{a}^{b} f(d - x) \, dx = \int_{d - b}^{d - a} f(x) \, dx$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_comp_sub_left
Description: For any real number $d$, the integral of the function $f(d - x)$ over the interval $[a, b]$ equals the integral of $f(x)$ over the interval $[d - b, d - a]$. That is,
