1. [THEOREM] Right cancellation property for invertible elements: $(a \cdot b)/b = a$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Invertible
Name: mul_div_cancel_of_invertible
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a type $\alpha$ equipped with multiplication and division, if $b$ is invertible (i.e., has a two-sided multiplicative inverse), then $(a \cdot b) / b = a$.
Signature:  (a b : α) [Invertible b] : a * b / b = a

2. [THEOREM] Fundamental Theorem of Calculus: $\int_a^b f' = f(b) - f(a)$ for continuous functions with pointwise derivative
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.FundThmCalculus
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDerivAt_of_le
Description: Let $a \leq b$ be real numbers, and let $f \colon [a, b] \to E$ be a continuous function on the closed interval $[a, b]$. Suppose that for every $x \in (a, b)$, the function $f$ has a derivative $f'(x)$ at $x$, and that $f'$ is integrable on $[a, b]$. Then:
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f'(y) \, dy = f(b) - f(a). \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hcont : ContinuousOn f (Icc a b)) (hderiv : ∀ x ∈ Ioo a b, HasDerivAt f (f' x) x)
  (hint : IntervalIntegrable f' volume a b) : ∫ y in a..b, f' y = f b - f a

3. [THEOREM] Fundamental Theorem of Calculus for Right-Differentiable Functions: $\int_a^b f' = f(b) - f(a)$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.FundThmCalculus
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_eq_sub_of_hasDeriv_right_of_le
Description: Let $a \leq b$ be real numbers, and let $f \colon [a, b] \to \mathbb{R}$ be a continuous function on the closed interval $[a, b]$. Suppose that for every $x \in (a, b)$, the function $f$ has a right derivative $f'(x)$ within the right neighborhood $(x, \infty)$, and that $f'$ is integrable on $[a, b]$. Then:
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f'(y) \, dy = f(b) - f(a). \]
Signature:  (hab : a ≤ b) (hcont : ContinuousOn f (Icc a b)) (hderiv : ∀ x ∈ Ioo a b, HasDerivWithinAt f (f' x) (Ioi x) x)
  (f'int : IntervalIntegrable f' volume a b) : ∫ y in a..b, f' y = f b - f a

4. [THEOREM] Division-Multiplication Cancellation: $(a / b) \cdot b = a$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic
Name: div_mul_cancel
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a group $G$, the operation $(a / b) \cdot b$ equals $a$.
Signature:  (a b : G) : a / b * b = a

5. [THEOREM] Fundamental Theorem of Calculus: $\int_a^b f' = f(b) - f(a)$ for differentiable functions on $\text{uIcc}(a, b)$
Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.FundThmCalculus
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_deriv_eq_sub
Description: Let $f \colon \mathbb{R} \to E$ be a function differentiable at every point in the closed interval $\text{uIcc}(a, b)$ (the smallest interval containing $a$ and $b$), and suppose its derivative $f'$ is integrable on $[a, b]$. Then:
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f'(y) \, dy = f(b) - f(a). \]
Signature:  (hderiv : ∀ x ∈ [[a, b]], DifferentiableAt ℝ f x) (hint : IntervalIntegrable (deriv f) volume a b) :
  ∫ y in a..b, deriv f y = f b - f a

6. [THEOREM] Right cancellation via division: $a \cdot (b / a) = b$
Module: Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic
Name: mul_div_cancel
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a group $G$, the operation $a \cdot (b / a)$ equals $b$, i.e., $a \cdot (b / a) = b$.
Signature:  (a b : G) : a * (b / a) = b
