Module: Mathlib.MeasureTheory.Integral.IntervalIntegral
Name: intervalIntegral.integral_nonneg
Description: For any real numbers $a \leq b$ and any function $f$, if $f(u) \geq 0$ for all $u$ in the closed interval $[a, b]$, then the interval integral of $f$ from $a$ to $b$ is nonnegative, i.e.,
\[ \int_{a}^{b} f(u) \, d\mu \geq 0. \]
