1. [THEOREM] Closed Interval as Insertion of Right Endpoint into Closed-Open Interval: $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \text{Ico}(a, b) \cup \{b\}$
Module: Mathlib.Order.Interval.Finset.Basic
Name: Finset.Icc_eq_cons_Ico
Description: For any elements $a$ and $b$ in a locally finite order $\alpha$ with $a \leq b$, the closed interval $[a, b]$ can be constructed by inserting the right endpoint $b$ into the closed-open interval $[a, b)$. Formally, $\text{Icc}(a, b) = \text{Ico}(a, b).\text{cons}(b, \text{right\_not\_mem\_Ico})$, where $\text{right\_not\_mem\_Ico}$ is the proof that $b \notin \text{Ico}(a, b)$.
Signature:  (h : a ≤ b) : Icc a b = (Ico a b).cons b right_not_mem_Ico

